#X obj 659 11 env.smooth~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 381 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A simple envelope with an exponential attack and release.
Unlike [env.ar~] \, both the attack and release use an exponential
curve instead of a linear one \, so the shape sounds smoother and more
natural \, especially for sustained sounds. The attack time and the
release time are the same and are controlled by a single @duration
property.;
#X text 240 199 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 224 • Smooth gating of a signal — fading a continuous sound
source (oscillator \, sample loop \, noise) in and out without clicks
or abrupt transitions.;
#X text 250 279 • Soft attack and release for pads — shaping long \,
sustained textures with a natural-sounding exponential contour \, so
that notes fade in and out smoothly.;
#X text 250 334 • Avoiding clicks when switching audio — muting and
unmuting a signal path with a short exponential ramp instead of a hard
on/off \, eliminating pops and clicks.;
#X text 250 389 • Simple percussive shaping — providing an exponential
decay tail for short percussive sounds \, giving them a natural \,
"acoustic" fade-out.;
